          "text": "🇪🇺 EU Parliament Freezes Mercosur Deal ⚖️🌍\nMEPs have voted to delay the EU-Mercosur trade agreement, referring it to the EU Court of Justice (ECJ) for a legal review, putting implementation on ice once again.\n\nThe vote was razor-thin: 46% in favour, 45% against, passing by just 10 MEPs.\n\n📊 By political group:\n🔹 ESN, PfE, The Left: Overwhelming support for sending the deal to the ECJ.\n🔹 Greens/EFA: More than two-thirds voted in favour of the referral.\n🔹 ECR: Nearly split down the middle, 46% yes, 49% no.\n🔹 Renew, S&D, EPP: Similar patterns, with around two-thirds voting no, but over 20% breaking ranks to vote yes.\n\n🔍 What does this vote do?\n• Suspends Parliament’s approval process for the Mercosur agreement.\n• Sends the deal to the ECJ to assess its compatibility with EU treaties.\n• Challenges the Commission’s decision to split the agreement and bypass national parliaments.\n• Raises legal questions over the deal’s “rebalancing mechanism.”\n\n⏳ The Court’s ruling could take over a year, leaving the deal frozen, though the Commission could still attempt provisional application, despite strong political resistance.\n\nWhat do you think is the future of this deal? 🤔\n\n#EU #Mercosur #TradePolicy #EUCourtOfJustice #EuropeanParliament #EUPolitics #Agriculture #Geopolitics"
        },
